<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Edward Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Île Saint-Jean</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Edward Island is the smallest province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-st-lawrence">Gulf of St. Lawrence</a>. Known to the French as Île Saint-Jean, it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1763, became a separate colony in 1769 and was renamed after Prince Edward, Duke of Kent, in 1799. Most of its land was granted to absentee proprietors, a grievance that shaped its politics until it joined Canada in 1873.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-edward-island.jpg" alt="Prince Edward Island" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: E Pluribus Anthony · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Prince_Edward_Island.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
